text=f"# Business signs coverage - v1.6.129\n\n{stats['renderedNames']} business names passed desktop and narrow-layout runtime checks: {stats['storefrontNames']} storefront signs and {stats['directoryNames']} names on {stats['directoryPanels']} shared-entrance directory panels. {coverage['unresolvedBusinesses']} catalogue records remain unresolved. This is a public-source catalogue, not proof that every real-world business is known.\n\nSource records: OpenStreetMap {coverage['sourceCounts'].get('osm',0)}; City of Peterborough {coverage['sourceCounts'].get('city-directory',0)}; Chamber {coverage['sourceCounts'].get('chamber-directory',0)}; DBIA/The Boro {coverage['sourceCounts'].get('boro-directory',0)}; ptbo.ca {coverage['sourceCounts'].get('ptbo-directory',0)}. Records with missing locations or unresolved duplicate identity remain in the audit; that count is not proof of additional physical businesses missing from the game. Each record retains source links and check dates. Directory pins require cross-source name/address corroboration or an exact municipal civic address on a property with one complete rendered building; conflicting or unsupported locations are retained in the unresolved audit. Raw footage, source images and raw directory markup are not published.\n\n{coverage.get('municipalCivicAddressMatches',0)} directory records have municipal civic-address/building corroboration. {coverage['municipalAddressFrontages']} storefronts use municipal property-address street evidence; {coverage['inferredNamedStreetWalls']} use an inferred nearest named street. Property primary addresses do not establish the exact tenant door.\n\nNames are wall-mounted in the opening band. Ordinary doors/windows and unsurveyed tenant positions remain inferred. Mall directory panels identify businesses in the building, rather than implying individual exterior shop entrances; mapped ground-floor shared-door IDs and positions are retained. Panels keep their 4.8 metre reading width, wall bounds and roof clearance. Untagged mall floor heights use an explicitly inferred 4.8 metre commercial storey; explicit heights and footage-reviewed profiles take precedence.\n\nGeometry/renderer regressions cover outward-facing text, neighbouring tenants, low roofs, map-mode round trips, editor hiding and shared entrance evidence. Front and both oblique approaches were captured across representative downtown and outlying buildings. Browser checks do not certify a physical phone. Shared atlas allocation: {stats['atlasBytes']//1048576} MiB.\n\nData: `city-explorer/data/business-directory.json`; unresolved records: `business-directory.coverage.json`. The broad business-completeness goal remains open while those records and additional source coverage need evidence.\n"
(root/"docs/business-signs-coverage.md").write_text(text,encoding="utf-8");print(json.dumps(coverage))
